WEBVTT

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.910
I share my unstoppable curiosity with you.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:17.710
I'm still able to run through the fog...

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:21.400
...because I know that you're here for me.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:29.130
I guess the shape of happiness is different for everyone...

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:33.470
...however, I know it's boring when I'm alone...

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:35.350
But, with you...

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:37.430
...it's like a mystery!

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:43.020
It's an enchanting future, where...

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:47.740
...in order for me to be strong, it's always you...

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:52.120
...that I can continue to depend on, right?

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:53.700
Just to survive!

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:55.660
Stumped Q? Don't lose your way!

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.500
Take this moment...

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:01.120
...to fix your gaze and charge on ahead!

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.330
Eternally, we'll always be together...

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.170
...searching and pursuing...

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:08.880
...the meaning of it all.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.010
Truth is nothing but a labyrinth...

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.720
...that we try to continue through...

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.390
...especially when we are hurt.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:18.560
I'll take you, so come this way.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:20.390
I'm certain that, on that day...

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:24.310
...I'll see your smile, face to face!

00:01:32.495 --> 00:01:35.531
Having joined Class A's special training…

00:01:35.765 --> 00:01:39.268
…we from Class Q are trying to
solve the unsolved case of…

00:01:39.268 --> 00:01:43.105
…Jack the Ripper and the double-door
closed room murder.

00:01:43.372 --> 00:01:46.008
That's why came to the Kirisaki Island,
where the case originally occurred.

00:01:47.076 --> 00:01:51.981
When we got to the scene where the details
of the case had been reproduced…

00:01:52.215 --> 00:01:55.151
…we found Saburoumaru-san's
corpse lying there, cut in half.

00:02:05.061 --> 00:02:05.995
Saburoumaru-san?

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:07.663
He's been cut in two!

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:18.941
It's Jack the Ripper…

00:02:20.142 --> 00:02:20.810
Dan-Sensei.

00:02:21.544 --> 00:02:27.149
It's almost the same as the previous case of Jack the
Ripper and the double-door closed room murder.

00:02:29.085 --> 00:02:31.187
The same thing that happened during
the case of Jack the Ripper…

00:02:31.487 --> 00:02:32.922
A closed room murder…

00:02:33.956 --> 00:02:34.924
It's exactly the same?

00:02:35.858 --> 00:02:40.096
What about the master key to the storeroom
that you said went missing yesterday?

00:02:40.896 --> 00:02:46.802
If they used that key to lock the two doors from the
outside, it's not really a closed room then, is it?

00:02:48.871 --> 00:02:49.572
Hey, everyone!

00:02:49.872 --> 00:02:50.806
What is it, Kyuu?

00:02:51.274 --> 00:02:52.108
Don't tell me it's another…

00:02:52.475 --> 00:02:53.309
Look at this!

00:02:57.313 --> 00:02:58.247
Could this key be…?

00:03:00.049 --> 00:03:03.886
Kyuu-kun, please try that key in the door lock.

00:03:12.428 --> 00:03:12.895
It works!

00:03:14.163 --> 00:03:15.031
What's going on here?

00:03:15.931 --> 00:03:19.935
If the missing master key was left here in the room…

00:03:21.103 --> 00:03:23.072
…it's a perfect closed room murder.

00:03:24.307 --> 00:03:28.010
This crime scene of a double door-closed room
murder you reproduced to test us…

00:03:28.511 --> 00:03:31.814
…has become a real murder scene, right?

00:03:32.114 --> 00:03:33.015
Dan-Sensei?

00:03:34.483 --> 00:03:36.652
Katagiri-kun, please call Maki-kun in here.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:40.790
Since he's our medical examiner, I
want him to examine the corpse.

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:41.590
Right away.

00:03:42.325 --> 00:03:43.793
Everyone else, please go back to your rooms.

00:03:44.493 --> 00:03:45.161
Understood.

00:03:51.233 --> 00:03:52.401
Megu, are you okay?

00:03:55.538 --> 00:03:56.305
I'm fine.

00:03:56.806 --> 00:04:00.876
If I get sick at each and every crime scene,
I won't be qualified to be a detective.

00:04:01.911 --> 00:04:02.712
I'm fine.

00:04:04.513 --> 00:04:06.682
If someone has a photographic memory…

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.852
…then that person can never forget what they saw.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:13.155
Like what happened back there.

00:04:14.323 --> 00:04:15.191
I feel sorry for her.

00:04:33.042 --> 00:04:36.445
Even though we weren't exactly on
best terms with Saburoumaru…

00:04:36.879 --> 00:04:38.247
…he didn't deserve that.

00:04:44.653 --> 00:04:46.355
Kinta, you're being careless.

00:04:47.356 --> 00:04:52.661
Saburoumaru was Megu's classmate back when
they were in the Ability Development Institute.

00:04:53.462 --> 00:04:54.530
Oh, that's right…

00:04:55.431 --> 00:04:58.134
But… Who would do such a thing?

00:04:58.467 --> 00:05:01.504
Well, we'll just have to figure it out. Isn't
this what a detective does anyway?

00:05:02.371 --> 00:05:04.740
You're saying all that but you're just
playing around with your computer!

00:05:05.207 --> 00:05:06.242
How rude!

00:05:06.675 --> 00:05:08.244
What have you been doing all this time?

00:05:09.111 --> 00:05:13.649
I'm looking for the murderer using
my very own detective software!

00:05:14.984 --> 00:05:22.258
When I input the details of the case it calculates
any possible tricks that could have been used.

00:05:23.692 --> 00:05:24.693
Does it really work?

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:26.362
Well, just take a look.

00:05:28.964 --> 00:05:31.700
Aren't you going about this the
wrong way, Kazuma-kun?

00:05:32.535 --> 00:05:33.302
Going about it wrong?

00:05:33.502 --> 00:05:34.370
What do you mean by that?

00:05:35.004 --> 00:05:36.705
The one who's careless is you.

00:05:37.606 --> 00:05:40.242
This is neither part of the training, nor is it a game.

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:42.511
It's a real murder case.

00:05:43.679 --> 00:05:44.847
Of course I know…!

00:05:44.847 --> 00:05:48.350
Aren't you pretty cold about the whole
thing yourself, Amakusa-kun?

00:05:51.787 --> 00:05:56.325
He may have been a stranger to you,
but to us, Saburoumaru was a friend.

00:05:57.059 --> 00:05:58.694
A friend has been killed…

00:05:59.962 --> 00:06:01.864
Someone from our school is dead, you know!

00:06:02.498 --> 00:06:04.433
Shouldn't that at least upset you?

00:06:07.036 --> 00:06:10.172
Is this really the time to be upset,
in a situation like this?

00:06:10.639 --> 00:06:11.173
What?

00:06:12.041 --> 00:06:13.476
Why don't you look out the window?

00:06:26.055 --> 00:06:26.956
Incredibly strong winds…

00:06:28.057 --> 00:06:29.558
It's probably going to start raining soon as well.

00:06:30.392 --> 00:06:31.927
The sea will be getting rough.

00:06:36.432 --> 00:06:40.002
Do you think a boat could sail in this weather?

00:06:46.075 --> 00:06:48.177
Then, do you mean…

00:06:48.844 --> 00:06:49.278
Exactly.

00:06:50.346 --> 00:06:52.915
For the time being, we won't be leaving this island.

00:06:54.116 --> 00:06:58.621
And the unidentified killer, Jack the
Ripper, is with us on this island.

00:07:04.293 --> 00:07:04.860
And what's more…

00:07:05.561 --> 00:07:08.264
The victim, Saburoumaru-san,
was a student of this school.

00:07:09.331 --> 00:07:12.968
The next victim could be anyone among us.

00:07:13.836 --> 00:07:16.572
We could be hacked to death in the same way.

00:07:28.884 --> 00:07:31.453
There's no way an outsider could've done this.

00:07:41.297 --> 00:07:42.898
Everyone, sorry to have kept you waiting.

00:07:43.265 --> 00:07:45.134
Dan-Sensei! Maki-Sensei!

00:07:45.968 --> 00:07:47.102
How's the boat?

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:51.540
Unfortunately, there's no way
we can leave in this storm.

00:07:52.041 --> 00:07:55.744
And due to the storm, the transmitter
on the cruiser isn't reaching.

00:07:56.412 --> 00:07:59.982
It seems that we're completely isolated here.

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:07.590
Everyone, with everything that's happened…

00:08:07.923 --> 00:08:09.458
And with us having no choice but to stay here…

00:08:10.859 --> 00:08:16.632
Even though you are all members of DDS, we do not
want to decide for you under these circumstances.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:23.138
A safe place inside this building has been prepared
for those of you unable to join in the investigation.

00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:27.610
Considering the situation, lessons have been halted.

00:08:28.811 --> 00:08:32.548
However, I'd still like to ask if
anyone of you would like to…

00:08:33.148 --> 00:08:41.690
…help us solve this case, and uncover
the identity of this Jack the Ripper.

00:08:43.792 --> 00:08:45.594
We'll do it. All of us from Class A.

00:08:47.062 --> 00:08:50.799
Even though we didn't know each other long, our
companion Saburoumaru-san was murdered!

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:52.668
There's no way we can let this go.

00:08:54.169 --> 00:08:57.940
Having said that, just leave it to us from Class A.

00:08:59.108 --> 00:09:01.677
Those from Class Q should remain
hidden somewhere safe.

00:09:02.811 --> 00:09:05.814
But you should all leave your badges
and notebooks behind.

00:09:09.218 --> 00:09:10.586
I'll do it, Dan-Sensei!

00:09:10.786 --> 00:09:12.521
Please let me help too!

00:09:14.486 --> 00:09:14.986
Kyuu...

00:09:15.924 --> 00:09:17.793
Alright! Count me in as well!

00:09:18.327 --> 00:09:18.961
Kinta!

00:09:19.461 --> 00:09:23.766
If I were frightened by this, I'd be bringing shame
upon my ancestors' sakura-snowstorm tattoo!

00:09:24.967 --> 00:09:27.069
Please let me help too.

00:09:27.536 --> 00:09:29.905
Well, obviously I'll help out too!

00:09:30.873 --> 00:09:33.275
Ryuu-kun, of course you'll help as well, right?

00:09:37.946 --> 00:09:38.681
Dan-Sensei!

00:09:39.381 --> 00:09:40.582
What's wrong, Katagiri-kun?

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:43.719
Something awful has happened in the kitchen!

00:09:54.296 --> 00:09:55.064
What's this?

00:09:55.764 --> 00:09:56.932
Everything's a mess.

00:09:57.766 --> 00:09:58.734
This is horrible…

00:09:59.968 --> 00:10:01.904
Damned mouse, get lost!

00:10:02.938 --> 00:10:05.340
Someone has messed up all the food.

00:10:07.009 --> 00:10:11.180
Does this mean that there's someone
else on this island?

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:13.115
I'm wondering about that as well.

00:10:26.862 --> 00:10:30.332
I see… That would mean…

00:10:36.805 --> 00:10:39.308
That's it! They used something like this!

00:10:39.942 --> 00:10:42.611
Kazuma, what have you been mumbling about?

00:10:43.812 --> 00:10:45.247
I understand now.

00:10:46.148 --> 00:10:49.651
The answer to how Jack the Ripper did what
he did in the double-door closed room.

00:10:49.918 --> 00:10:51.253
Eh? Are you serious?

00:10:51.854 --> 00:10:52.688
Really?

00:10:55.524 --> 00:10:58.594
Now, shall I show you how the
same thing can be done?

00:10:59.428 --> 00:11:03.732
I'll show you how the murderer did
what he did in the closed room.

00:11:04.633 --> 00:11:07.536
On the rooftop where it happened…

00:11:09.271 --> 00:11:10.405
On the rooftop…

00:11:22.352 --> 00:11:24.054
Ah! Such strong winds!

00:11:25.922 --> 00:11:28.492
Hey, Kazuma, are you really sure about this?

00:11:28.825 --> 00:11:29.660
Of course I am!

00:11:30.494 --> 00:11:34.798
Geez, why am I tagging along for the
deduction of a mere grade schooler?

00:11:35.198 --> 00:11:37.901
Eh, is that distress I hear?

00:11:38.568 --> 00:11:42.606
Since I came up with the answer
before Class A and all…

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:43.774
What'd you say?

00:11:45.042 --> 00:11:46.910
Our classmate was killed.

00:11:47.277 --> 00:11:48.545
Don't tell us such nonsense!

00:11:52.916 --> 00:11:56.186
The interior room in which we found
Saburoumaru-san's corpse was…

00:11:56.386 --> 00:11:59.489
…without a doubt, a double-door closed room.

00:12:01.491 --> 00:12:07.331
There is a small window that faces the cliff,
but a person couldn't go through it.

00:12:07.831 --> 00:12:12.302
But then, the culprit wasn't the only one who
could enter and leave the closed room.

00:12:13.337 --> 00:12:15.639
Take the mice around here for example.

00:12:16.206 --> 00:12:16.907
Mice?

00:12:19.910 --> 00:12:22.446
Excuse me, could you please close the door?

00:12:25.682 --> 00:12:26.883
Take a look around.

00:12:27.551 --> 00:12:29.252
There should be some place where light can come in.

00:12:39.696 --> 00:12:42.733
There's a mouse hole in the corner of the front door.

00:12:51.875 --> 00:12:54.745
…the space of the gap underneath this
second door is about 6.8 cm in height.

00:12:55.579 --> 00:13:00.317
So, the interior room where the body was
found wasn't actually a closed room…

00:13:01.818 --> 00:13:06.523
Because there are holes that anything the size
of a mouse or smaller can pass through.

00:13:06.957 --> 00:13:11.228
Hey now, don't tell me you're going to
say that the mice carried the body in?

00:13:12.262 --> 00:13:17.401
No, what I meant to say was, the key to
this storeroom is smaller than a mouse.

00:13:17.968 --> 00:13:19.703
So that means… What?

00:13:20.003 --> 00:13:24.174
That means, after the murderer used the
stolen master key to exit the room…

00:13:24.574 --> 00:13:28.645
…he slid the key back inside via the mouse
hole and the gap under the door.

00:13:28.979 --> 00:13:30.414
Umm, is that what you think?

00:13:31.448 --> 00:13:33.083
Is that all you wanted to say?

00:13:34.351 --> 00:13:36.353
I'm the one known as the puzzle king.

00:13:37.053 --> 00:13:39.823
I would've thought of such a simple trick already.

00:13:45.962 --> 00:13:47.864
Hey, Goudo-san, what do you think you're…

00:13:48.331 --> 00:13:49.366
Let me borrow your feet for a bit.

00:13:50.434 --> 00:13:52.135
Let's think of this this 5-yen coin as the key.

00:13:53.136 --> 00:13:57.741
First, let's attach string to the key and bang it
on to something that's near the target area.

00:13:59.042 --> 00:14:01.211
After that, I'll draw the string steadily…

00:14:02.045 --> 00:14:07.818
…and when it comes near the target location,
it'll draw back into a single thread.

00:14:08.552 --> 00:14:09.586
I get it now!

00:14:10.654 --> 00:14:14.724
But Kyuu-kun found the key in a corner of this room.

00:14:15.792 --> 00:14:19.129
There wasn't anything that would serve
the purpose of that girl's legs there.

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:20.931
Exactly.

00:14:21.731 --> 00:14:24.401
If there's nothing for the string
to catch on, it won't work.

00:14:25.702 --> 00:14:28.672
If you want something to catch on,
let me show you how to do it.

00:14:29.372 --> 00:14:29.873
What?

00:14:32.943 --> 00:14:36.279
We can use this counter-weight
from the balance in the kitchen.

00:14:37.247 --> 00:14:41.418
First we tie a string to the weight, place it at
the target location, then close the door.

00:14:42.285 --> 00:14:45.622
When the key hits the weight, it drops off.

00:14:46.523 --> 00:14:51.761
After the key falls, the weight can be retrieved
by pulling the string tied to it.

00:14:53.163 --> 00:14:55.632
And with that, the riddle of the double-door
closed room is solved.

00:15:01.104 --> 00:15:04.040
Now, thinking of the 5-yen coin as the key again…

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:06.676
…I'll demonstrate returning the
key through the interior door.

00:15:07.844 --> 00:15:10.046
We draw the string slowly…

00:15:25.629 --> 00:15:26.463
Is something the matter?

00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:28.865
It seems to be stack onto something.

00:15:30.767 --> 00:15:32.369
Is it okay if I do it over?

00:15:44.548 --> 00:15:46.082
Huh?? Darn it…

00:15:47.117 --> 00:15:47.651
Again?

00:15:48.251 --> 00:15:49.853
This is more trouble than I thought…

00:15:50.754 --> 00:15:52.622
I seem to be doing something wrong.

00:15:56.359 --> 00:15:58.328
It should've all worked out smoothly…

00:15:59.896 --> 00:16:01.431
This is so weird…

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:07.938
I think I got it this time!

00:16:09.938 --> 00:16:11.207
Yes!

00:16:11.207 --> 00:16:12.075
It's a success!

00:16:12.375 --> 00:16:15.145
But it took you about 30 minutes.

00:16:16.079 --> 00:16:19.849
Look, the 5-yen coin should be in front of
the interior door where the weight was!

00:16:24.921 --> 00:16:27.023
If you're looking for the 5-yen coin, it's right here.

00:16:27.958 --> 00:16:30.226
No matter how you look at it,
it's closer the front entrance.

00:16:32.362 --> 00:16:36.700
Well, the weight moved a bit, but
it was more or less accurate.

00:16:37.367 --> 00:16:39.603
After all, it's been put back into the closed room.

00:16:45.075 --> 00:16:45.775
I understand now.

00:16:46.676 --> 00:16:51.848
Thinking in terms of a pivot object and then
trying to feed it back is not a bad idea.

00:16:52.248 --> 00:16:53.183
Dan-Sensei…

00:16:53.817 --> 00:16:57.020
But in a place like this storeroom…

00:16:57.187 --> 00:17:00.523
…there are many objects which can block this
technique of drawing an object along with string.

00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:02.892
Just like now, every time we tried It ended in failure.

00:17:04.094 --> 00:17:11.701
Additionally, if the weight moves, because the room
is locked, you can't try again like you did.

00:17:12.435 --> 00:17:19.042
Let alone the fact that the key was in the
interior room beyond the second door.

00:17:19.509 --> 00:17:23.613
In that case, the probability of
success is very nearly zero.

00:17:24.414 --> 00:17:28.051
But what if the culprit had just gambled
on that small chance…

00:17:28.818 --> 00:17:34.224
Unfortunately, there's another reason that proves
the method you've just described is impossible.

00:17:35.792 --> 00:17:36.893
Katagiri-kun, the key.

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:40.830
Take a closer look.

00:17:41.765 --> 00:17:46.269
Do you think it's possible to use the method which
you've just demonstrated on this key?

00:17:48.271 --> 00:17:51.741
There's no hole! So you can't thread it…

00:17:52.342 --> 00:17:56.012
Well, well, looks like you're only
up to this level after all.

00:17:56.546 --> 00:17:58.314
So this is as far as Class Q can go.

00:17:59.182 --> 00:17:59.783
Let's head back.

00:18:00.283 --> 00:18:01.951
Yeah, what a waste of our time.

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:04.354
Kazuma…

00:18:25.842 --> 00:18:26.443
Kazuma-kun.

00:18:28.278 --> 00:18:29.112
Your deduction…

00:18:29.979 --> 00:18:32.015
…may not be completely wrong.

00:18:43.893 --> 00:18:44.627
Everyone…

00:18:46.396 --> 00:18:48.164
It's really nothing to get so upset about!

00:18:48.498 --> 00:18:49.132
That's right!

00:18:49.466 --> 00:18:51.267
It was a pretty well thought-out answer.

00:18:51.701 --> 00:18:53.136
Let's all try again and do our best together.

00:18:53.403 --> 00:18:53.937
Okay?

00:19:01.845 --> 00:19:05.381
Even though he may seem to be very
strong he's still a kid, after all.

00:19:06.616 --> 00:19:08.551
78 cm, B cup.

00:19:09.686 --> 00:19:12.122
You're not as flat as I first thought you were!

00:19:14.691 --> 00:19:15.492
Hey, Kazuma!

00:19:16.192 --> 00:19:16.860
Don't run off!

00:19:17.093 --> 00:19:18.128
You're just envious!

00:19:20.263 --> 00:19:21.364
Are you really a B cup?

00:19:22.632 --> 00:19:25.568
Wow, all this while I thought you were an A cup…

00:19:29.172 --> 00:19:31.174
Hey, wait for me, Megu!

00:19:30.473 --> 00:19:31.241
Go away!

00:19:39.015 --> 00:19:39.783
Well, now.

00:19:40.183 --> 00:19:43.653
Maki-Sensei, please read out
the result of the autopsy.

00:19:44.487 --> 00:19:44.921
Alright.

00:19:44.921 --> 00:19:47.624
First, the cause of death.

00:19:48.958 --> 00:19:51.895
The victim succumbed to a knife wound to the heart, likely from a sharp blade

00:19:52.829 --> 00:19:54.864
Most likely, the death was instant.

00:19:55.832 --> 00:19:57.967
After Saburoumaru-kun's death,
the murderer seems…

00:19:58.101 --> 00:20:02.305
…to have used either a chainsaw or some other
powerful tool to separate the body into two.

00:20:03.173 --> 00:20:07.777
The chainsaw we think may have been used is missing from the equipment room.

00:20:08.978 --> 00:20:10.980
The time of death was during
the second half of the night.

00:20:11.548 --> 00:20:15.351
According to the state of his digested dinner,
it would be approximately 2:00 am.

00:20:16.553 --> 00:20:20.056
Saburoumaru-kun's right half has
still not been found as of yet.

00:20:33.403 --> 00:20:34.070
Who's there?

00:20:34.838 --> 00:20:36.439
It's me, Ryuu.

00:20:37.273 --> 00:20:38.074
Ryuu-kun?

00:20:38.942 --> 00:20:40.577
What are you doing up so late at night?

00:20:41.911 --> 00:20:44.681
I need to talk to you. Open up.

00:20:45.582 --> 00:20:46.349
Wait a sec.

00:20:48.785 --> 00:20:50.320
What do you want to talk about?

00:20:52.088 --> 00:20:52.789
The truth is…

00:20:55.058 --> 00:20:56.926
You're getting in my way.

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:07.570
A dream…

00:21:08.538 --> 00:21:10.974
What a dream to have!

00:21:11.341 --> 00:21:12.609
I'm so hopeless!

00:21:16.012 --> 00:21:18.648
I did seem to hear someone knocking on my door.

00:21:25.555 --> 00:21:26.623
What huge footprints!

00:21:27.023 --> 00:21:28.324
Someone really was here!

00:21:30.493 --> 00:21:31.594
And they're heading that way…

00:21:32.795 --> 00:21:33.730
What should I do?

00:21:34.063 --> 00:21:35.365
Maybe it's better if I called somebody…

00:21:37.433 --> 00:21:41.471
No, I can't. I can't be a detective if I
have to call someone else like this.

00:21:42.572 --> 00:21:44.107
Alright! Time to get a move on, Kyuu!

00:22:08.364 --> 00:22:09.065
What's going on?

00:22:16.439 --> 00:22:17.840
Did he go into that room?

00:22:19.175 --> 00:22:22.111
Alright! Let's open the door and see
who you really are, Jack the Ripper!

00:22:24.948 --> 00:22:27.784
I think maybe calling Kinta would've
been better, after all.

00:22:31.788 --> 00:22:32.522
K-Kinta!

00:22:32.655 --> 00:22:34.524
Hey, hey, what are you doing here?

00:22:36.392 --> 00:22:39.095
You appeared right there out of the blue! I
thought you might've been Jack the Ripper!

00:22:40.697 --> 00:22:45.234
So you came here after someone knocked on your
door and you followed the footprints too?

00:22:45.802 --> 00:22:47.637
Huh?? You, too?

00:22:48.338 --> 00:22:53.009
Yeah. No matter how you look at it, these muddy
footprints don't belong to any of us.

00:22:54.177 --> 00:22:56.045
And the footprints disappear in front of that room.

00:22:59.582 --> 00:23:00.183
Let's go, Kyuu.

00:23:00.917 --> 00:23:02.018
Y-yeah…

00:23:08.491 --> 00:23:09.792
So, he escaped through the window.

00:23:13.463 --> 00:23:14.430
Is something wrong, Kinta?

00:23:22.105 --> 00:23:24.774
The upper-half of Shishido-san's body
appeared on the bed out of nowhere.

00:23:25.441 --> 00:23:30.213
His last visage was one of peace,
as if he was still sleeping.

00:23:36.640 --> 00:23:47.570
Unable to cry in front of you, I'm whistling instead.

00:23:50.280 --> 00:24:02.130
Saying "I'll always be beside you" without saying a single word.

00:24:02.130 --> 00:24:09.220
My loving heart is overflowing; those sad thoughts...

00:24:09.220 --> 00:24:14.850
are like things that fade away unnoticed in mid-air.

00:24:15.050 --> 00:24:21.060
And again, with a mighty smile of relief...

00:24:21.190 --> 00:24:26.610
I will see you off.

00:24:26.860 --> 00:24:36.450
Goodbye and thank you.

00:24:38.546 --> 00:24:40.982
We've finally begin to unravel the riddle
of the double-door closed room…

00:24:41.249 --> 00:24:44.019
…through the sharp deduction of the
talented bishounen, Amakusa Ryuu.

00:24:44.753 --> 00:24:46.888
What is the secret that could change
the impossible to possible?

00:24:47.122 --> 00:24:47.555
However…

00:24:48.089 --> 00:24:49.858
The killings haven't come to an end yet.

00:24:50.592 --> 00:24:52.861
We, the members of DDS, have made up our minds.

00:24:53.561 --> 00:24:54.562
There's only one answer!

00:24:56.698 --> 00:25:00.168
The truth is, the hints needed to unravel the
double-door closed room trick are all present.

00:25:00.702 --> 00:25:02.637
The way the 5-yen coin rolled backwards…

00:25:03.571 --> 00:25:04.973
The place where the key was…

00:25:05.740 --> 00:25:08.276
And the food missing from the kitchen…

00:25:09.077 --> 00:25:10.545
Oh my, are you making a cake?
